Typo in Lecture Notes #4
\fs26 \cf3 \expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\
In Table 1, at the end of Lecture Notes #4, there is a typo for the posterior mean of sigma^2 when using a scaled inverse chi-square distribution. The entry in the lower right hand corner of the table is the posterior scale parameter (not the posterior mean!) and needs to be multiplied by nu_n/(nu_n-2) to obtain the posterior mean. The correct expression for the posterior mean is nu_n s_n^2 / (nu_n - 2) = (nu_0 s_0^2 + nv) / (nu_0 + n - 2).\
\

